WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.008 --> 00:00:00.841
(gentle music)

00:00:00.841 --> 00:00:02.700
- [Narrator] Before the Spanish conquest

00:00:03.730 --> 00:00:05.453
and before the Inca empire,

00:00:06.650 --> 00:00:08.900
one group created the most important

00:00:08.900 --> 00:00:13.843
South American civilization
at the time, the Chimu.

00:00:16.940 --> 00:00:20.390
The Chimu civilization lasted
almost half a millennium,

00:00:20.390 --> 00:00:24.233
from the year 1000 to around 1470 A.D.

00:00:26.360 --> 00:00:28.930
At its height, the
kingdom spanned the region

00:00:28.930 --> 00:00:31.000
between the southern border of Ecuador

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:33.283
and the Peruvian capital of Lima.

00:00:34.460 --> 00:00:37.330
Much of the Chimus' success has
to do with their engineering

00:00:37.330 --> 00:00:39.823
capabilities and artistry.

00:00:41.449 --> 00:00:45.310
The Chimu were able to
construct massive structures,

00:00:45.310 --> 00:00:49.470
particularly in the wealthy
capital city of Chan Chan.

00:00:49.470 --> 00:00:53.230
Thousands of adobe structures,
such as palaces and temples,

00:00:53.230 --> 00:00:55.210
were up to hundreds of feet long,

00:00:55.210 --> 00:00:58.793
and some of those buildings
had walls about 30 feet high.

00:01:01.480 --> 00:01:04.763
The Chimu also developed a
signature artistic style.

00:01:05.640 --> 00:01:08.560
Craftsmen excelled at
producing luxury textiles

00:01:08.560 --> 00:01:10.230
and elaborate metalworks.

00:01:11.561 --> 00:01:15.640
They also created ceramics
that were distinctly Chimu

00:01:15.640 --> 00:01:18.920
and often reflected aspects
of their coastal lifestyle,

00:01:18.920 --> 00:01:21.603
such as fish, otters, and sea birds.

00:01:23.900 --> 00:01:26.620
Despite advancements
in art and engineering,

00:01:26.620 --> 00:01:29.930
the Chimu civilization eventually fell.

00:01:29.930 --> 00:01:34.210
By around 1470 A.D., they were
conquered by the next great

00:01:34.210 --> 00:01:37.053
Andean civilization, the Inca.

00:01:40.720 --> 00:01:44.343
Centuries later, however,
the Chimu culture lives on.

00:01:45.220 --> 00:01:48.190
In 1986, Chan Chan was designated

00:01:48.190 --> 00:01:52.130
a UNESCO World Heritage Site,
helping preserve the legacy

00:01:52.130 --> 00:01:56.415
of this ancient culture for
many more years to come.

00:01:56.415 --> 00:01:59.665
(gentle guitar music)

